<title>PORTUGAL: BPI-SGPS to raise capital total 60 bln esc.</title>
<headline>BPI-SGPS to raise capital total 60 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento -SGPS (BPI) said on Wednesday it was raising its capital by 30 billion escudos for shareholders and issuing a further 30 billion escudos of preferential non-voting shares.</p>
<p>BPI-SGPS's capital currently stands at 56.45 billion escudos.</p>
<p>The group, which is in the process of acquiring state-controlled Banco de Fomento e Exterior (BFE), said the increases would take place over the next six months.</p>
<p>BPI offered 2,615 escudos per share in its successful bid for the 65 percent of BFE on offer.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
